d{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-16I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6eff25-c0fc-5cff-b89a-ea3df60bc57a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 