tep 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-5I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90fb4001-d74b-5e2d-81b4-e24b882a4776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371390} {:answer/id #uuid "71ce610f-82ae-522c-926e-b7c2ee6f0d39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371391} {:answer/id #uuid "4b580747-f003-59f3-9a6e-264464d07479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371392} {:answer/id #uuid "cde90a24-0864-55d6-88d1-1399a2d4ca92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371393} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2ea819-e496-5d30-a827-efe68e69aeae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371393} :answer-field/id #uuid "db5a28ad-71bd-5130-9bc2-0a90bb411ead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371389}] :question/id #uuid "c0e502e2-3a05-5080-ba55-d3ba7ba5d628" :question/math-academy-id "q-96427" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-6I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fbafe0-bf41-5b20-aac4-0695ff6118ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385888} {:answer/id #uuid "b87a58a7-40d4-5cee-b379-768117d0434b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385889} {:answer/id #uuid "8d10f141-9b73-597a-9894-f347066824f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385890} {:answer/id #uuid "3455f0ca-75c2-537a-9f24-93cc9bc1292f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385891} {:answer/id #uuid "6377c93b-2085-5845-a870-b47edaf10db1"