tors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{20}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{20}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{20}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{20}}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$ \n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{20} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{20}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6fa92bb-2f31-59f3-b917-55e7960a18b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404845} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f1a295-1a1b-5b5c-bafa-3d4d8db7586d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404846} {:answer/id #uuid "15013ea