\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{10}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-10I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{10} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{10}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2161ac8-52f4-5d9a-92a3-77afc2763246" :answe